WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.839 --> 00:00:07.229
Combined with his power as well as the deep
care he shows for his family, he is one of

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:18.269
the most popular membesr of the crew in all
of Whole cake Island.

00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:23.470
On top of all this, Katakuri also introduces
us to the concept of future sight, a very

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:28.640
advanced form of Kenbunshoku Haki, that allows
him to look several seconds ahead into the

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:34.780
future and react accordingly, a skill so rare
that it’s not even shared by his Mother

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.120
Big Mom.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:42.341
And so overall, when Luffy manages to pull
Katakuri into a 1 vs 1 fight in the mirror

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:48.340
world to enable his crew’s escape, naturally
we all anticipated this battle to be one of

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:53.530
the most challenging ones for Luffy so far,
against an antagonist that seems extremely

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.030
rational and calculated.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:09.599
And what follows is one the best battles and
character arcs in the story so far.

00:01:09.599 --> 00:01:13.909
This is where the main theme of Katakuri’s
character comes into play.

00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:18.970
And it’s actually so important, that it
will serve as the overarching framework for

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:25.129
this entire character analysis.

00:01:25.129 --> 00:01:29.890
Mirrors.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:34.320
Everything about Katakuri is reflected in
the symbol of the mirror.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.060
On the smallest level, this can be seen in
terms of his future sight, that is all about

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.890
looking ahead and seeing things that you usually
can’t, just like you use a mirror to look

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.519
around corners.

00:01:46.519 --> 00:01:57.990
And just like a mirror, your future sight
can be blurred when loosing composure.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:05.629
But I honestly think it’s so much more interesting
to look at this symbol on a much larger scale.

00:02:05.629 --> 00:02:11.860
Because the main implication here, is that
Katakuri and Luffy mirror each other as characters

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.319
on more than just one way.

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:19.569
To really understand to what extend Oda has
created Katakuri as a mirrored version of

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:30.409
Luffy, I think it’s best to peel away the
layers one by one.

00:02:30.409 --> 00:02:36.580
On the most superficial level, Luffy and Katakuri
are similar simply based on their devil fruit

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.940
powers.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:43.410
While Luffy is made of Rubber, Katakuri is
made of Mochi a malleable sort of rice cake

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.990
that can easily change its shape.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:51.749
This is not the first time that Oda has shown
us a villain with a smiler over to Luffy’s.

00:02:51.749 --> 00:02:57.360
Thinking back to before the time-skip, Bellamy
was also quite similar to Luffy’s ability

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.140
in terms of speed and bounciness.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:06.830
The purpose of this trope is to have the protagonist
‘fight and overcome himself’ and thus

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:10.760
give us an idea where he stands in terms of
his power development.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:16.540
In Bellamy’s case we saw that Luffy was
actually way stronger than him, which was

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:21.339
in line with his up-and-coming rookie status
before the Alabasta Arc.

00:03:21.339 --> 00:03:25.430
Katakuri however shows us the exact opposite.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:30.030
While his powers are even more similar to
Luffy’s, his message at the beginning of

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:35.660
the fight is clear: Whatever you can do with
your devil fruit, I can do better.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:41.710
And so we learn very quickly that the underlying
subtext of this battle is for Luffy to overcome

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:45.040
himself and increase his fighting abilities.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.100
In other words, this was the first battle
where, in line with Rayleigh’s explanation

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:55.649
on Ruskaina, he will have to become stronger
DURING a battle, compared to training beforehand

00:03:55.649 --> 00:04:04.440
as he did for instance against Lucci.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:10.290
And what makes this battle against Katakuri
so unique from Luffy’s perspective, is the

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.700
incentive for it.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:18.750
You see, in almost every single major battle,
Luffy’s victory ends in the liberation of

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:24.960
the people oppressed by villain, as he’s
fighting for their sake.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:30.929
Luffy defeating Arlong meant freed Nami and
her village form her oppression.

00:04:30.929 --> 00:04:36.149
Taking out Crocodile meant the end of the
civil war and suffering in Alabasta.

00:04:36.149 --> 00:04:40.990
And when Luffy punched Doflamingo down into
the ground it literally cut the strings that

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:43.010
were controlling Dressrosa.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:48.649
It’s this pattern that usually makes his
fights so satisfying to see.

00:04:48.649 --> 00:04:53.750
Against Katakuri however, Luffy doesn’t
free Whole Cake Island or the Big Mom pirates

00:04:53.750 --> 00:05:02.460
from the Yonko’s rage and tyranny.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:06.249
Beating Katakuri wouldn’t change the country
itself.

00:05:06.249 --> 00:05:11.850
And since Luffy had already retrieved Sanji
and protected his crew by shutting himself

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:17.690
into the mirror world together with Katakuri,
there was no-one to liberate or rescue.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:23.059
And so suddenly, his battle and relationship
with katakuri moved to a much more personal

00:05:23.059 --> 00:05:29.040
level, that was about personal power and ideology,
for the very first time being fully able to

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.690
focus on himself and his own ambitions.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:45.660
This I think is what makes Katakuri so different
and unique in the story.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.920
So here we have the main objective for LUFFY.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:54.709
However, moving down yet another layer, Luffy
and Katakuri mirror each other not only on

00:05:54.709 --> 00:06:05.179
a physical level, but on a personal level
as well.

00:06:05.179 --> 00:06:09.670
And this is where we get to the really interesting
part of this video.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:14.920
As we slowly learn over the course of their
fight, Katakuri’s cool and composed demeanour

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:18.420
starts to crack and slowly fall apart.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:25.920
Both him and Luffy have crazily similar personalities,
only that Katakuri has built up this false

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:29.660
persona over time in the hope to protect his
family.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:36.980
In his flashback we see a happy and careless
boy, that is unapologetic about who he is.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:42.790
When Perespero tells him that his life would
be easier if he simply covered his mouth,

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:47.709
Katakuri answers that he doesn't care what
others think about him and that he would beat

00:06:47.709 --> 00:06:50.470
up anyone if necessary.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:59.520
The 
second trait we notice about him, is his strong

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.320
protective nature when it comes to his family.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:07.740
This strongly reminds us of the Luffy we know
today.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:20.200
He only adopts his "perfect" persona when
Brulee was attacked because of him.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:24.430
He lost his true self to the desire to protect
his family.

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:29.750
We actually saw a similar moment in Luffy's
life after Ace's death were he lost faith

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.360
in himself.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.700
Luckily however, he had Jinbei in that moment
to set him straight.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:40.400
Unfortunately for Katakuri though, he didn't
have someone like that within the ranks of

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.550
his quite unloving family.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:48.440
Therefore he adopted this new persona, to
protect his loved ones.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:59.610
We can also see this discrepancy really well
during the Marienda scene.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:03.870
While Luffy doesn’t care looking weak in
front of his friends, as we see in his encounter

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:11.120
with Sanji, nor about showing happiness and
enjoyment, Katakuri literally puts walls around

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:17.490
him to keep anyone from seeing his love for
lying down and eating Doughnuts.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:23.380
Luffy has to break down those literal walls
for him to wake him up to the loneliness he’s

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.380
in.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:29.790
Despite being a well-respected member of the
biggest family in the world, nobody understands

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:33.200
him and knows who he really is at heart.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:37.940
And so, I believe that what really sparked
Katakuri’s interest and initial anger when

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:43.760
facing off against Luffy, was the fact that
he saw himself and his lost potential reflected

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:44.760
in Luffy.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:48.650
And so he had to prove to himself that he
made the right decision in hiding his true

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:51.180
self and covering up his face.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:57.261
Thus, at the beginning of the fight, the emphasis
wasn't just on "I am stronger than you" but

00:08:57.261 --> 00:09:06.900
rather it was "Everything you do, I do better."

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:13.130
I believe that his excuse that Luffy will
be a danger to Big mom that needs to be eliminated,

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.900
was only a part of his motivation.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:20.150
And so the fight became much more personal
for Katakuri has well.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:25.880
As a result we have a fight of two people
who are incredibly involved with each other,

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:30.820
one fighting to reach his potential in terms
of power and the other in terms of character.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:36.960
And I think the resilience and will Luffy
demonstrates to ultimately beat Katakuri,

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:41.860
are also wonderfully reflected by their similar
devil fruit powers as well.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:48.970
While Katakuri is Mochi that when pounded
stays as it is, Luffy being Rubber always

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:58.560
bounces back and can’t be squashed.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:04.730
This fantastic thematic concept, combined
with a compelling multi-layered personality

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:10.290
is what gives Katakuri’s character this
intimate and likeable feel, that is quite

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:12.860
unique in the story so far.

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:26.070
Both Luffy and Katakuri make the other reflect
on themselves and their respective weaknesses.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:32.010
As a result, the battle is one of the best
sequences of character crafting and character

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:38.360
development at the same time, mixing great
physical growth on Luffy’s part with great

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:41.610
psychological growth on Katakuri’s.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:47.280
As their fight progresses, Katakuri gains
more and more respect for Luffy.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:11:14.170
This is evident in the shift of language used
as Katakuri now is saying things like or . He

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:18.660
starts to admire Luffy’s resilience and
the rapid development of his future sight

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:20.020
skills.

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:25.810
It reaches a point where both are fighting
at full strength, but both also seem to be

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.680
enjoying their duel.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:33.290
This becomes especially clear in the iconic
scene where Katakuri stabs himself to make

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.340
up for the wound he inflicted to Luffy after
Flampe’s interference.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:42.950
The fact that both of them take her and the
other onlookers out of the picture with conquerors

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:54.020
Haki makes the relationship between the two
even better.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:12:00.070
At this point Luffy has convinced Katakuri
that being yourself and living authentically

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:05.620
is important, not only for your own happiness
and growth, but also for that of the people

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.600
around you.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:14.320
Better to be understood &amp; accepted by few,
like Brûlée rather then admired for pretending

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:18.430
to be someone else by someone like Flampe.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:29.960
Thus Katakuri throws off his scarf and starts
embracing his true self again.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:35.410
And so, while both fight at full strength,
his motives change.

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:42.340
At this point, Katakuri has a direct interest
in Luffy actually winning and proving that

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.730
he can be his true self.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:55.150
In a way, Luffy defeating him, would set him
free from the facade

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:57.770
he has built.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:03.660
And so, while I believe that Luffy fairly
beat Katakuri in terms of strength, he made

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:08.940
it a point to fall on his back, showing Luffy
his respect for his growth, while at the same

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:13.730
time breaking the biggest aspect of his old,
fake self.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:19.570
Now, his character has changed completely
form the cold and calculated villain to a

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:26.100
compassionate and honourable antagonist, that
has now developed a liking towards Luffy.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:32.420
And so, bringing this back to what we talked
about earlier, what makes this fight so different

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:38.670
is that Luffy is not liberating someone from
the antagonist, but in this case liberates

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.780
the antagonist himself.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:46.530
This culminates in the heartwarming scene
after the end of the fight, as Brulee tended

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:54.380
to her brothers wounds.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:14:00.280
She knew perfectly well, that Katakuri had
fallen willingly on his back, and when Katakuri

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:06.130
asked about Luffy, Brúlée guessed that he
would be pleased to know that Luffy escaped

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.740
Totto Land.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:11.440
Katakuri smirked, confirming her assumption.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:18.950
And so, in the end it was only Brûlées of
all people, who cared the most for her brother’s

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:21.200
true self &amp; suffering.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:27.560
And bringing the theme full circle, it was
her that with her mirror powers enabled his

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:36.810
and Luffy’s change in the first place.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:42.830
As a result I think it is more than fair to
argue, that while Luffy won the overall battle,

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:48.030
Katakuri went out of this fight as a true
winner himself, having regained his sense

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:52.920
of self and being pulled from his loneliness
and isolation.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:58.220
It sets him up to become relevant again in
the story and makes him one of my favourite

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:07.410
antagonists in all of One Piece.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:11.630
If you feel like watching a little longer,
I really recommend checking out some of my

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:14.420
other character analyses right here.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:17.230
Thanks guys.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.669
Peace.

